    {
      "id": "Ht84aiRT7-cAnoJ1emHl8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 810.838680536895,
      "y": -3023.8702973615636,
      "width": 895.287109375,
      "height": 2475,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bLA",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1922317840,
      "version": 2492,
      "versionNonce": 440208815,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1748282768280,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "p : point d'intersection entre le rayon et le cylindre\ns : origine du rayon\nD : vecteur direction du rayon normalisé\nt : scalaire >= 0\n\np = D * t + s\n\n\nSoit V la direction du cylindre normalisée\n\nV ⋅ V = ||V|| * ||V|| * cos(V, V)\nV ⋅ V = 1 * 1 * 1\nV ⋅ V = 1\n\nDe la meme maniere, D ⋅ D = 1\n\n\nSoit c le centre du cylindre (extrémité du cylindre)\nSoit a le centre du cercle dans lequel p est inclus\nSoit m ∈ |R\n\na = c + m * V\n\nCA = a - c\nCA = c + m * V - c\nCA = m * V\n\nV et AP sont orthogonaux\nDonc AP ⋅ V = 0\n(CA - CA + AP) ⋅ V = 0\n(CA + AP - CA) ⋅ V = 0\n(CP - CA) ⋅ V = 0\n(CP - m * V) ⋅ V = 0\nCP ⋅ V - m * V ⋅ V = 0\nCP ⋅ V - m = 0\nm = CP ⋅ V\n\n\nSoit r le rayon du cylindre\n\nr = ||AP||\nr = ||AC + CP||\nr = ||CP + AC||\nr = ||CP - CA||\nr = ||CP - m * V||\nr² = ||CP - m * V||²\n\nSoit X un vecteur\n||X|| = sqrt(X ⋅ X) = sqrt(X²)\n||X||² = X ⋅ X = X²\n\nr² = (CP - m * V)²\nr² = [CP - V * (CP ⋅ V)]²\nr² = CP² - 2 * [(CP  ⋅ (V * [CP ⋅ V])] + [V * (CP ⋅ V)]²\nr² = CP² - 2 * [(CP ⋅ V) * (CP ⋅ V)] + V² * (CP ⋅ V)²\nr² = CP² - 2 * (CP ⋅ V)² + 1 * (CP ⋅ V)²\nr² = CP² - (CP ⋅ V)²\nr² = (p - c)² - [(p - c) ⋅ V]²\nr² = (D * t + s - c)² - [(D * t + s - c) ⋅ V]²\nr² = (D * t + CS)² - [(D * t + CS) ⋅ V]²\nr² = CS² + 2 * (CS ⋅ [D * t]) + (D * t)² - [(D * t) ⋅ V + CS ⋅ V]²\nr² = CS² + 2 * (CS ⋅ [D * t]) + (D * t)² - [(D * t) ⋅ V + CS ⋅ V]²\nr² = CS² + 2 * t * (CS ⋅ D) + D² * t² - [(D ⋅ V) * t + CS ⋅ V]²\nr² = CS² + 2 * t * (CS ⋅ D) + 1 * t² - ([(D ⋅ V) * t]² + 2 *  (D ⋅ V) * t * (CS ⋅ V) + (CS ⋅ V)²)\nr² = CS² + 2 * t * (CS ⋅ D) + 1 * t² - [(D ⋅ V) * t]² - 2 *  (D ⋅ V) * t * (CS ⋅ V) - (CS ⋅ V)²\nr² = CS² + 2 * t * (CS ⋅ D) + t² - (D ⋅ V)² * t² - 2 *  (D ⋅ V) * t * (CS ⋅ V) - (CS ⋅ V)²\nr² = t² - (D ⋅ V)² * t² + 2 * t * (CS ⋅ D) - 2 *  (D ⋅ V) * t * (CS ⋅ V) + CS² - (CS ⋅ V)²\nr² = [1 - (D ⋅ V)²] * t² + 2 * t * [(CS ⋅ D) -  (D ⋅ V) * (CS ⋅ V)] + CS² - (CS ⋅ V)²\n0 = [1 - (D ⋅ V)²] * t² + 2 * t * [(CS ⋅ D) -  (D ⋅ V) * (CS ⋅ V)] + CS² - (CS ⋅ V)² - r²\n\nOn doit donc résoudre l'équation quadratique défini par :\na = 1 - (D ⋅ V)²\nb = 2 * [(CS ⋅ D) -  (D ⋅ V) * (CS ⋅ V)]\nc = CS² - (CS ⋅ V)² - r²\n\n\nSi le point C n'est pas sur une extrémitée mais est le centre du cylindre,\nil peut etre utile d'utiliser le centre des 2 extrémitées et de préparer des calculs à l'avance.\nSoit b le centre du \"bas\" du cylindre, t celui du \"haut\" et hh la moitié de sa hauteur.\nbs ⋅ V = (s - b) ⋅ V\nbs ⋅ V = [s - (c - hh * V)] ⋅ V\nbs ⋅ V = (s - c + hh * V) ⋅ V\nbs ⋅ V = (CS + hh * V) ⋅ V\nbs ⋅ V = CS ⋅ V + hh * V ⋅ V\nbs ⋅ V = CS ⋅ V + hh\n\nD'apres le meme raisonnement,\nts ⋅ V = CS ⋅ V - hh\n\nPour calculer la normal du point d'intersetion :\nn = AP\nn = AC + CP\nn = CP - CA\nn = CP - V * m\n\nAttention, si D ⋅ n > 0, alors la camera se trouve à l'intérieur du cylindre donc\nn = -(CP - V * m)\n\nn devra sans doute etre normalisé pour la suite.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "p : point d'intersection entre le rayon et le cylindre\ns : origine du rayon\nD : vecteur direction du rayon normalisé\nt : scalaire >= 0\n\np = D * t + s\n\n\nSoit V la direction du cylindre normalisée\n\nV ⋅ V = ||V|| * ||V|| * cos(V, V)\nV ⋅ V = 1 * 1 * 1\nV ⋅ V = 1\n\nDe la meme maniere, D ⋅ D = 1\n\n\nSoit c le centre du cylindre (extrémité du cylindre)\nSoit a le centre du cercle dans lequel p est inclus\nSoit m ∈ |R\n\na = c + m * V\n\nCA = a - c\nCA = c + m * V - c\nCA = m * V\n\nV et AP sont orthogonaux\nDonc AP ⋅ V = 0\n(CA - CA + AP) ⋅ V = 0\n(CA + AP - CA) ⋅ V = 0\n(CP - CA) ⋅ V = 0\n(CP - m * V) ⋅ V = 0\nCP ⋅ V - m * V ⋅ V = 0\nCP ⋅ V - m = 0\nm = CP ⋅ V\n\n\nSoit r le rayon du cylindre\n\nr = ||AP||\nr = ||AC + CP||\nr = ||CP + AC||\nr = ||CP - CA||\nr = ||CP - m * V||\nr² = ||CP - m * V||²\n\nSoit X un vecteur\n||X|| = sqrt(X ⋅ X) = sqrt(X²)\n||X||² = X ⋅ X = X²\n\nr² = (CP - m * V)²\nr² = [CP - V * (CP ⋅ V)]²\nr² = CP² - 2 * [(CP  ⋅ (V * [CP ⋅ V])] + [V * (CP ⋅ V)]²\nr² = CP² - 2 * [(CP ⋅ V) * (CP ⋅ V)] + V² * (CP ⋅ V)²\nr² = CP² - 2 * (CP ⋅ V)² + 1 * (CP ⋅ V)²\nr² = CP² - (CP ⋅ V)²\nr² = (p - c)² - [(p - c) ⋅ V]²\nr² = (D * t + s - c)² - [(D * t + s - c) ⋅ V]²\nr² = (D * t + CS)² - [(D * t + CS) ⋅ V]²\nr² = CS² + 2 * (CS ⋅ [D * t]) + (D * t)² - [(D * t) ⋅ V + CS ⋅ V]²\nr² = CS² + 2 * (CS ⋅ [D * t]) + (D * t)² - [(D * t) ⋅ V + CS ⋅ V]²\nr² = CS² + 2 * t * (CS ⋅ D) + D² * t² - [(D ⋅ V) * t + CS ⋅ V]²\nr² = CS² + 2 * t * (CS ⋅ D) + 1 * t² - ([(D ⋅ V) * t]² + 2 *  (D ⋅ V) * t * (CS ⋅ V) + (CS ⋅ V)²)\nr² = CS² + 2 * t * (CS ⋅ D) + 1 * t² - [(D ⋅ V) * t]² - 2 *  (D ⋅ V) * t * (CS ⋅ V) - (CS ⋅ V)²\nr² = CS² + 2 * t * (CS ⋅ D) + t² - (D ⋅ V)² * t² - 2 *  (D ⋅ V) * t * (CS ⋅ V) - (CS ⋅ V)²\nr² = t² - (D ⋅ V)² * t² + 2 * t * (CS ⋅ D) - 2 *  (D ⋅ V) * t * (CS ⋅ V) + CS² - (CS ⋅ V)²\nr² = [1 - (D ⋅ V)²] * t² + 2 * t * [(CS ⋅ D) -  (D ⋅ V) * (CS ⋅ V)] + CS² - (CS ⋅ V)²\n0 = [1 - (D ⋅ V)²] * t² + 2 * t * [(CS ⋅ D) -  (D ⋅ V) * (CS ⋅ V)] + CS² - (CS ⋅ V)² - r²\n\nOn doit donc résoudre l'équation quadratique défini par :\na = 1 - (D ⋅ V)²\nb = 2 * [(CS ⋅ D) -  (D ⋅ V) * (CS ⋅ V)]\nc = CS² - (CS ⋅ V)² - r²\n\n\nSi le point C n'est pas sur une extrémitée mais est le centre du cylindre,\nil peut etre utile d'utiliser le centre des 2 extrémitées et de préparer des calculs à l'avance.\nSoit b le centre du \"bas\" du cylindre, t celui du \"haut\" et hh la moitié de sa hauteur.\nbs ⋅ V = (s - b) ⋅ V\nbs ⋅ V = [s - (c - hh * V)] ⋅ V\nbs ⋅ V = (s - c + hh * V) ⋅ V\nbs ⋅ V = (CS + hh * V) ⋅ V\nbs ⋅ V = CS ⋅ V + hh * V ⋅ V\nbs ⋅ V = CS ⋅ V + hh\n\nD'apres le meme raisonnement,\nts ⋅ V = CS ⋅ V - hh\n\nPour calculer la normal du point d'intersetion :\nn = AP\nn = AC + CP\nn = CP - CA\nn = CP - V * m\n\nAttention, si D ⋅ n > 0, alors la camera se trouve à l'intérieur du cylindre donc\nn = -(CP - V * m)\n\nn devra sans doute etre normalisé pour la suite.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
