    {
      "id": "LQZtjSMnNE1CnsHOSJM2P",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3077.838680536895,
      "y": -3024.3702973615636,
      "width": 1199.3114013671875,
      "height": 3300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bM5",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 568652525,
      "version": 5298,
      "versionNonce": 1435137285,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1749659625798,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "p : point d'intersection entre le rayon et le cone\ns : origine du rayon\nD : vecteur direction du rayon normalisé\nt : scalaire >= 0\n\np = D * t + s\n\n\nSoit V la direction du cone normalisée\n\nV ⋅ V = ||V|| * ||V|| * cos(V, V)\nV ⋅ V = 1 * 1 * 1\nV ⋅ V = 1\n\nDe la meme maniere, D ⋅ D = 1\n\n\nSoit c la pointe du cone \nSoit a le centre du cercle dans lequel p est inclus\nSoit m ∈ |R\n\na = c + m * V\n\nCA = a - c\nCA = c + m * V - c\nCA = m * V\n\nV et AP sont orthogonaux\nDonc AP ⋅ V = 0\n(CA - CA + AP) ⋅ V = 0\n(CA + AP - CA) ⋅ V = 0\n(CP - CA) ⋅ V = 0\n(CP - m * V) ⋅ V = 0\nCP ⋅ V - m * V ⋅ V = 0\nCP ⋅ V - m = 0\nm = CP ⋅ V\nm = (p - c) ⋅ V\nm = (D * t + s - c) ⋅ V\nm = (D * t + CS) ⋅ V\nm = D ⋅ V * t + CS ⋅ V\n\nSoit i le centre de l'extrémité du cone\nSoit j l'intersection de la droite (cp) et de l'extrémité du cone\nSoit le triangle cij\np ∈ (cj)\na ∈ (ci)\nD'apres le théoreme de Thales\n||CA|| / ||CI|| = ||CP|| / ||CJ|| = ||AP|| / ||IJ||\n\n||AP|| / ||IJ|| = ||CA|| / ||CI||\n||AP|| = ||CA|| * ||IJ|| / ||CI||\n||AP|| = ||m * V|| * ||IJ|| / ||CI||\n||AP|| = ||m * V|| * ||IJ|| / ||CI||\n||AP|| = m * ||V|| * ||IJ|| / ||CI|| car m est forcément positif\n||AP|| = m * ||IJ|| / ||CI||\n\n\nSoit X un vecteur quelconque\n||X|| = sqrt(X ⋅ X) = sqrt(X²)\n||X||² = X ⋅ X = X²\n\nOn pose k = ||IJ|| / ||CI||\nm * k = ||AP||\n(m * k)² = ||AP||²\n(m * k)² = AP²\nm² * k² = (p - a)²\nm² * k² = (p - c - m * V)²\nm² * k² = (CP - m * V)²\nm² * k² = CP² - 2 * CP ⋅ [V * m] + (m * V)²\nm² * k² = CP² - 2 * [CP ⋅ V] * m + (m * V)²\n0 = CP² - 2 * m * m + (m * V)² - m² * k²\n0 = CP² - 2 * m² + m² * V² - m² * k²\n0 = CP² - 2 * m² + m² * 1 - m² * k²\n0 = CP² + m² * (-2 + 1 - k²)\n0 = CP² + m² * (-1 - k²)\n0 = CP² - m² * (1 + k²)\n0 = (p - c)² - m² * (1 + k²)\n0 = (D * t + s - c)² - (D ⋅ V * t + CS ⋅ V)² * (1 + k²)\n0 = (D * t + CS)² - ([D ⋅ V * t]² + 2 * [D ⋅ V * t] * [CS ⋅ V] + [CS ⋅ V]²) * (1 + k²)\n0 = (D * t)² + 2 * (D * t) ⋅ CS + CS² - ([D ⋅ V]² * t² + 2 * [D ⋅ V] * [CS ⋅ V] * t + [CS ⋅ V]²) * (1 + k²)\n0 = D² * t² + 2 * (D ⋅ CS) * t  + CS² - ([D ⋅ V]² * [1 + k²] * t² + 2 * [1 + k²] * [D ⋅ V] * [CS ⋅ V] * t + [CS ⋅ V]² * [1 + k²])\n0 = 1 * t² + 2 * (D ⋅ CS) * t  + CS² - [D ⋅ V]² * [1 + k²] * t² - 2 * [1 + k²] * [D ⋅ V] * [CS ⋅ V] * t - [CS ⋅ V]² * [1 + k²]\n0 = (1 - [D ⋅ V]² * [1 + k²]) * t² + 2 * ([D ⋅ CS] - [1 + k²] * [D ⋅ V] * [CS ⋅ V]) * t - (CS ⋅ V)² * (1 + k²) + CS²\n\nOn doit donc résoudre l'équation quadratique défini par :\na = 1 - [D ⋅ V]² * [1 + k²]\nb = 2 * ([D ⋅ CS] - [1 + k²] * [D ⋅ V] * [CS ⋅ V])\nc = - (CS ⋅ V)² * (1 + k²) + CS²\n\n\n\nIl peut etre utile de calculer (IS ⋅ V) pour d'autre calculs\nSoit h la hauteur du cone\nIS ⋅ V = (s - i) ⋅ V\nIS ⋅ V = (s - [c + h * V]) ⋅ V\nIS ⋅ V = (s - c - h * V) ⋅ V\nIS ⋅ V = (CS - h * V) ⋅ V\nIS ⋅ V = CS ⋅ V - h * V ⋅ V\nIS ⋅ V = CS ⋅ V - h\n\n\nPour calculer la normal du point d'intersetion :\nLa somme des angles d'un triangle est 180 degrés\ndonc 180 = angle(pca) + angle(cap) + angle(apc)\n180 = f + 90 + e\n90 = f + e\n\nDe meme pour le triangle cpj\nOr cpa = qpj\nDonc qpu = f\n\nOr k = ||IJ|| / ||CI||\nk = tan(f)\nk = tan(angle(qpu))\nk = ||QU|| / ||QP||\nk = ||QU|| / ||AP||\nk * ||AP|| = ||QU||\nk * m * ||IJ|| / ||CI|| = ||QU||\nk² * m = ||QR||\n\nn = PU\nn = PQ + QU\nn = AP + QU\nn = AP + ||QU|| * (-V)\nn = p - a - V * k² * m\nn = p - c - m * V - V * k² * m\nn = CP - m * V (1 + k²)\n\nAttention, si D ⋅ n > 0,    alors la camera se trouve à l'intérieur du cone donc\nn = -[CP - m * V (1 + k²)]\n\nn devra sans doute etre normalisé pour la suite.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "p : point d'intersection entre le rayon et le cone\ns : origine du rayon\nD : vecteur direction du rayon normalisé\nt : scalaire >= 0\n\np = D * t + s\n\n\nSoit V la direction du cone normalisée\n\nV ⋅ V = ||V|| * ||V|| * cos(V, V)\nV ⋅ V = 1 * 1 * 1\nV ⋅ V = 1\n\nDe la meme maniere, D ⋅ D = 1\n\n\nSoit c la pointe du cone \nSoit a le centre du cercle dans lequel p est inclus\nSoit m ∈ |R\n\na = c + m * V\n\nCA = a - c\nCA = c + m * V - c\nCA = m * V\n\nV et AP sont orthogonaux\nDonc AP ⋅ V = 0\n(CA - CA + AP) ⋅ V = 0\n(CA + AP - CA) ⋅ V = 0\n(CP - CA) ⋅ V = 0\n(CP - m * V) ⋅ V = 0\nCP ⋅ V - m * V ⋅ V = 0\nCP ⋅ V - m = 0\nm = CP ⋅ V\nm = (p - c) ⋅ V\nm = (D * t + s - c) ⋅ V\nm = (D * t + CS) ⋅ V\nm = D ⋅ V * t + CS ⋅ V\n\nSoit i le centre de l'extrémité du cone\nSoit j l'intersection de la droite (cp) et de l'extrémité du cone\nSoit le triangle cij\np ∈ (cj)\na ∈ (ci)\nD'apres le théoreme de Thales\n||CA|| / ||CI|| = ||CP|| / ||CJ|| = ||AP|| / ||IJ||\n\n||AP|| / ||IJ|| = ||CA|| / ||CI||\n||AP|| = ||CA|| * ||IJ|| / ||CI||\n||AP|| = ||m * V|| * ||IJ|| / ||CI||\n||AP|| = ||m * V|| * ||IJ|| / ||CI||\n||AP|| = m * ||V|| * ||IJ|| / ||CI|| car m est forcément positif\n||AP|| = m * ||IJ|| / ||CI||\n\n\nSoit X un vecteur quelconque\n||X|| = sqrt(X ⋅ X) = sqrt(X²)\n||X||² = X ⋅ X = X²\n\nOn pose k = ||IJ|| / ||CI||\nm * k = ||AP||\n(m * k)² = ||AP||²\n(m * k)² = AP²\nm² * k² = (p - a)²\nm² * k² = (p - c - m * V)²\nm² * k² = (CP - m * V)²\nm² * k² = CP² - 2 * CP ⋅ [V * m] + (m * V)²\nm² * k² = CP² - 2 * [CP ⋅ V] * m + (m * V)²\n0 = CP² - 2 * m * m + (m * V)² - m² * k²\n0 = CP² - 2 * m² + m² * V² - m² * k²\n0 = CP² - 2 * m² + m² * 1 - m² * k²\n0 = CP² + m² * (-2 + 1 - k²)\n0 = CP² + m² * (-1 - k²)\n0 = CP² - m² * (1 + k²)\n0 = (p - c)² - m² * (1 + k²)\n0 = (D * t + s - c)² - (D ⋅ V * t + CS ⋅ V)² * (1 + k²)\n0 = (D * t + CS)² - ([D ⋅ V * t]² + 2 * [D ⋅ V * t] * [CS ⋅ V] + [CS ⋅ V]²) * (1 + k²)\n0 = (D * t)² + 2 * (D * t) ⋅ CS + CS² - ([D ⋅ V]² * t² + 2 * [D ⋅ V] * [CS ⋅ V] * t + [CS ⋅ V]²) * (1 + k²)\n0 = D² * t² + 2 * (D ⋅ CS) * t  + CS² - ([D ⋅ V]² * [1 + k²] * t² + 2 * [1 + k²] * [D ⋅ V] * [CS ⋅ V] * t + [CS ⋅ V]² * [1 + k²])\n0 = 1 * t² + 2 * (D ⋅ CS) * t  + CS² - [D ⋅ V]² * [1 + k²] * t² - 2 * [1 + k²] * [D ⋅ V] * [CS ⋅ V] * t - [CS ⋅ V]² * [1 + k²]\n0 = (1 - [D ⋅ V]² * [1 + k²]) * t² + 2 * ([D ⋅ CS] - [1 + k²] * [D ⋅ V] * [CS ⋅ V]) * t - (CS ⋅ V)² * (1 + k²) + CS²\n\nOn doit donc résoudre l'équation quadratique défini par :\na = 1 - [D ⋅ V]² * [1 + k²]\nb = 2 * ([D ⋅ CS] - [1 + k²] * [D ⋅ V] * [CS ⋅ V])\nc = - (CS ⋅ V)² * (1 + k²) + CS²\n\n\n\nIl peut etre utile de calculer (IS ⋅ V) pour d'autre calculs\nSoit h la hauteur du cone\nIS ⋅ V = (s - i) ⋅ V\nIS ⋅ V = (s - [c + h * V]) ⋅ V\nIS ⋅ V = (s - c - h * V) ⋅ V\nIS ⋅ V = (CS - h * V) ⋅ V\nIS ⋅ V = CS ⋅ V - h * V ⋅ V\nIS ⋅ V = CS ⋅ V - h\n\n\nPour calculer la normal du point d'intersetion :\nLa somme des angles d'un triangle est 180 degrés\ndonc 180 = angle(pca) + angle(cap) + angle(apc)\n180 = f + 90 + e\n90 = f + e\n\nDe meme pour le triangle cpj\nOr cpa = qpj\nDonc qpu = f\n\nOr k = ||IJ|| / ||CI||\nk = tan(f)\nk = tan(angle(qpu))\nk = ||QU|| / ||QP||\nk = ||QU|| / ||AP||\nk * ||AP|| = ||QU||\nk * m * ||IJ|| / ||CI|| = ||QU||\nk² * m = ||QR||\n\nn = PU\nn = PQ + QU\nn = AP + QU\nn = AP + ||QU|| * (-V)\nn = p - a - V * k² * m\nn = p - c - m * V - V * k² * m\nn = CP - m * V (1 + k²)\n\nAttention, si D ⋅ n > 0,    alors la camera se trouve à l'intérieur du cone donc\nn = -[CP - m * V (1 + k²)]\n\nn devra sans doute etre normalisé pour la suite.",
